      "message": "CI: prereleases of dev from a `next` branch (npm dist-tag `next`) (#191)\n\n* CI: prereleases of dev from a `next` branch under the npm dist-tag `next`\n\nThe publish workflow runs on master, next and lane/rNNN. One check before the build (channel-guard, was lane-guard)\nholds every unpublished version to its branch: a prerelease with publishConfig.tag `next` on next, `three-rNNN` on a\nlane, and a release version without a publishConfig.tag on master, so a prerelease or a dist-tag merged by mistake\ndoes not publish to latest. CONTRIBUTING: Prereleases.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EWN5WHZ5NrRUojD2GpjigT\n\n* Docs: installing a prerelease with plugins (npm overrides), per-package changelogs, stale `next` tag\n\nnpm never counts a prerelease as matching a plugin's peer range (`>=0.6.0`), so\n`npm i threepipe@next` with any plugin fails with ERESOLVE. Getting started now shows the\n`\"overrides\": {\"threepipe\": \"$threepipe\"}` fix. CONTRIBUTING: each package's own CHANGELOG.md,\nversion bumps that a `dev` merge brings along, and moving the `next` dist-tag after a release.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EWN5WJVoif5u2R5D96ps9b\n\n* Docs: the prerelease install note moves from Getting started to a new FAQ page\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EWN5WJVoif5u2R5D96ps9b\n\n* test:types: the consumer project overrides threepipe with the packed core, so a prerelease core installs\n\nA prerelease (0.7.0-next.0, 0.7.0-r172.1) never matches plugin-tweakpane's peer range `threepipe: >=0.4.0`, so the\nconsumer check's npm install stopped with ERESOLVE and every release from `next` or a lane would stop in post-build\n(Codex on #191). Same override the FAQ gives to users. Checked with npm's resolver (--dry-run) on the 0.6.0 tarball\nrelabelled 0.7.0-next.0 and plugin-tweakpane 0.10.1: exit 1 without the override, 0 with it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EWN5WHZ5NrRUojD2GpjigT\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Palash Bansal <palash@shaders.app>",
